nd visual sciences. Established in 2007, the college has consistently delivered top-tier academic training and clinical exposure to students aspiring to become professional optometrists and vision scientists. Affiliated with The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, the institute combines rigorous classroom instruction with hands-on practice in state-of-the-art diagnostic laboratories and vision clinics.\\n\\nThe curriculum is structured to cover fundamental and advanced concepts in clinical optometry, contact lenses, low vision care, binocular vision, and ocular disease management. The faculty comprises seasoned ophthalmologists, clinical optometrists, and researchers who mentor students through experiential learning and evidence-based patient care practices. The campus features specialized darkrooms, advanced refraction units, and dedicated research facilities to foster innovation in eye healthcare.\\n\\nBeyond academics, SJSIO actively engages in community outreach programs, organizing free eye screening camps, rural vision care drives, and public awareness campaigns on eye health. With strong institutional tie-ups with leading eye hospitals and optical chains, students benefit from robust internship placements and career opportunities globally, making it a preferred destination for optometry studies in South India.","highlights":["Dedicated institution for optometry and visual sciences","Affiliated with The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Advanced clinical labs equipped with modern diagnostic tools","Experienced faculty panel of ophthalmologists and optometrists","Regular community outreach and rural eye screening camps","Strong placement network with top eye hospitals and brands","Comprehensive hands-on clinical training from first year","Separate hostel facilities for male and female students","Active participation in national optometric conferences","Well-stocked specialized library with global research journals"],"departments":[{"name":"Bachel